WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.801
Let's talk about

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.602
all this

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.570
cancel culture

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.104
and stuff

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.039
that you've been writing a lot about.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.440
What I want to ask you is,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.041
is it

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:11.144
particularly troubling issue for you

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.746
as a comedian?

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.448
Because, I mean, at some level, isn't

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.985
isn't every joke in some way offensive

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.988
Yeah, you're right.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.323
You're trying to hate you.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.958
I mean, absolutely not.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.659
For every comedian, most comedians

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.294
don't go near anything that's offensive.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.296
It's just not the way they work.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.231
It's just not it's

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.432
not the kind of material

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.166
that interests them.

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.568
They're talking about other things.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.302
Me? Yes.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.037
This is

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.938
obviously

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.840
has always been an issue with me.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.841
And

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:42.842
it's

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.210
but it's not just

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.245
people in show business,

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.347
not just such as famous people anymore

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.848
who worry about cancel culture.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.583
There are a lot of people,

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.051
I don't know,

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.018
going through their high school

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:52.919
yearbook, like,

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:53.720
oh, my God, did

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.555
I wear a sombrero and

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.723
the prop or something?

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:57.490
And I mean,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.591
lots of regular

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.727
people have been canceled for things,

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:01.961
you know, some guy says.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:04.597
I don't know, just just

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.099
something he thinks is innocuous.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.634
It's he doesn't know

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.134
He's saying,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.636
well, white lives matter, too,

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.404
and he doesn't quite understand.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.939
He's not of that generation

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.241
why we want a particular focus,

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.142
because black lives

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.211
have always been more at peril.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.279
There's a reason

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.281
why that was a saying

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.916
and became an organization.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.050
And he gets canceled.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.119
Nobody just sat down and said, hey, hey,

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:26.853
this, this, this.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.155
And he might I went, Oh, okay. I get it.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.790
No, you're just gone.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.524
That's what

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.159
people are just very tired

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.295
of walking on eggshells in this country.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.596
That is something

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.931
the Democrats are also fighting

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.066
in this election. People don't like it.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.603
And, you know, this is also part of why

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:44.971
Elon Musk taking over

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.339
Twitter is just such

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.740
an enormous controversy

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.042
with so many people.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:52.045
And 99% of Twitter employees

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.446
voted Democratic.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.914
Even if you're a Democrat,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.916
you shouldn't think that's a good thing.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.351
To have a major

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.120
what really is a news organization,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.688
because people get their news from the

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.123
but from someplace

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.290
where the entire

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.892
organization thinks one way.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.194
That's the very definition of groupthink.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.162
Part of the problem is

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.396
we are sorting ourselves

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.531
into these two tribes

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.800
and it feels like college education

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.736
and urban rural are the two big dividers

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.072
where maybe religion would be the third.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.707
So you get these urban,

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.142
college educated,

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.977
secular people on one side

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.478
and you get rural,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.913
more religious

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.982
less and less college education.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.118
And there's just so much tribal

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.020
suspicion, hostility,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.621
you know,

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.588
it feels as if

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.624
it's not really about issues anymore.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.391
You know, it's

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.292
no, I keep

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.560
trying to tell people who,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.895
you know, don't even want to breathe

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.197
the same air as a Trump voter.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.232
Like you can hate Trump

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:46.900
you can't hate

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.035
all the people who voted for him.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.503
It's half the country.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:51.437
And on top of that,

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.773
I really believe I have always believed

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:54.941
being conservative

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.310
is a personality

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.213
trait before it's a political position.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.082
It's just something that's very innate.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.918
You know, think of some uncle you had.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:05.852
He was a great guy.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.954
You loved him, but he was just a concert.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.022
It was just in his blood.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.190
Like, some people are neat

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.457
and some people are messy

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.226
and some people are adventurous

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.228
and some people are cautious.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.462
It's just a personality.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.331
And then the politics comes in later.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.033
That's some of it has to do with religion

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.434
and where you live in the way

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.503
you were brought up and stuff like that.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.204
But I mean,

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.004
there are just people

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.973
who are going to be conservative

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.208
and you're going to have to live

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:28.708
with them.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.177
You can't own them or destroy them.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.745
They're not going to self-deport

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:33.246
and they're about

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.048
to take over the government

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.883
so they're not going to give it back.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.184
So what is going to happen

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:39.786
is let's assume both houses

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.821
go go Republican, where there's

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.855
this is what I was saying

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.190
at the end of my show Friday.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.325
I felt the audience was

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:46.559
stunned, as they should be,

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:48.394
but they shouldn't be

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.262
because it's been going on

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:49.996
for a long time.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.831
And I've been saying it for a long time.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:52.232
Yes.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:55.568
I mean, unless there's a

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.437
oddity with the polling

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.772
and it's going to be a very good day

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.474
for the Republicans,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.776
as we both have mentioned,

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.511
the majority of Republicans

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.747
running for Congress,

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.082
for Senate, for House

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.817
and for statehouses,

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.852
the people who are going to decide

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.988
who is the president in 20, 24

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.589
are election deniers.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.592
They don't believe in this crazy idea

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.628
that the guy with the most vote wins.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.631
So what happens in 2024 is Trump

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.898
is going to try the coup

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.233
he tried in 2020

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.735
which was plainly an attempted coup.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.403
There's no other way to look at it

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.572
but this time he's going to have in place

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.541
this army of deniers who will support him

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.278
and he is going to show up Robert to do.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.879
I will bet every money

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.482
bit of money I have he will show up

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.817
on inauguration day on 2025

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.452
whether he's the winner or not.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.787
And then we'll see what happens

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.856
and then we'll see how much we look like

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.791
other countries that we thought

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.393
oh that could never happen to us.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.662
Yeah, it could and that could.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:56.929
And he may have

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.666
thousands of people with arms as he did.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.434
January 6th.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.635
You think they're going to stay home

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:03.569
now that

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:05.238
this has happened again

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.906
and they have all these people in

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.341
place that are on their side?

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.144
Oh, no, my friend.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:14.314
It's going to be very interesting.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.883
On that cheery note, Bill,

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.551
I wish I had better news to report,

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.385
but you asked me.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.486
Thank you for doing that. Right?

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.587
My pleasure. Always.

